CSpake2: SPAKE2 over edwards25519 for ADB Wi-Fi pairing (DroidDrive plan P3-02)

Origin
------
Copied from BoringSSL, https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl,
tag 0.20240913.0 (commit 58f3bc83230d2958bb9710bc910972c4f5d382dc), the last
releases where these files were still C:

  crypto/curve25519/curve25519.c         -> curve25519.c
  crypto/curve25519/spake25519.c         -> spake25519.c
  crypto/curve25519/curve25519_tables.h  -> curve25519_tables.h
  crypto/curve25519/internal.h           -> curve25519_internal.h
  third_party/fiat/curve25519_64.h       -> fiat_curve25519_64.h

Each file keeps its original copyright and licence header. The full licence
texts are LICENSE.boringssl (BoringSSL's LICENSE file; the files above are
under its ISC-style "Google Inc." licence) and LICENSE.fiat (MIT, fiat-crypto
authors).

Changes made for DroidDrive
---------------------------
- The #include lines of the four C files were replaced by
  `#include "boringssl_shim.h"` plus the local file names above. No other line
  of BoringSSL's code was changed.
- boringssl_shim.h is new. It holds the few BoringSSL helpers these files use:
  the constant-time functions copied verbatim from crypto/internal.h, generic
  bn_add_words/bn_select_words, SHA-512 mapped to CommonCrypto, RAND_bytes
  mapped to arc4random_buf, and #defines that prefix every exported symbol with
  "cspake2_"/"CSPAKE2_" so this copy cannot clash with another BoringSSL in the
  process (Network.framework ships one).
- include/cspake2.h (the public header) and cspake2_test_hook.c are new
  DroidDrive files, not BoringSSL code.

